<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<title>Thomson's plum pudding model</title>
<style>
  :root{
    --bg: #ffffff;
    --card: #ffffff;
    --border: #222222;
    --text: #111111;
    --muted: #555555;
    --green: #2e7d32;
    --blue: #1a56b0;
  }
  *{box-sizing:border-box;}
  body{
    margin:0;
    font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,sans-serif;
    background:#faf9f6;
    color:var(--text);
    padding:32px 16px 60px;
  }
  .wrap{max-width:760px;margin:0 auto;}
  h1{font-size:24px;font-weight:600;margin:0 0 6px;}
  .sub{color:var(--muted);font-size:14px;margin:0 0 24px;}

  .card{
    background:var(--card);
    border:1px solid #ddd;
    border-radius:14px;
    padding:20px;
    margin-bottom:24px;
    position:relative;
  }

  .controls{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:12px;margin-top:14px;}
  button{
    border:1px solid #222;
    background:#111;
    color:#fff;
    border-radius:8px;
    padding:9px 18px;
    font-size:14px;
    cursor:pointer;
  }
  button:active{transform:scale(0.98);}
  .hint{font-size:12px;color:var(--muted);}

  h2{font-size:17px;font-weight:600;margin:0 0 10px;}
  p{font-size:15px;line-height:1.7;margin:0 0 14px;}
  ul{margin:0 0 14px;padding-left:20px;font-size:15px;line-height:1.7;}

  .t{font-size:14px;fill:var(--text);font-family:inherit;}
  .ts{font-size:12px;fill:var(--muted);font-family:inherit;}
  .th{font-size:14px;font-weight:600;fill:var(--text);font-family:inherit;}

  .watermark{
    position:absolute;
    bottom:10px;
    right:14px;
    font-size:11px;
    color:#999;
    opacity:0.6;
    user-select:none;
    pointer-events:none;
  }

  @keyframes drift1 { 0%,100%{transform:translate(0,0);} 50%{transform:translate(2px,-3px);} }
  @keyframes drift2 { 0%,100%{transform:translate(0,0);} 50%{transform:translate(-3px,2px);} }
  @keyframes drift3 { 0%,100%{transform:translate(0,0);} 50%{transform:translate(3px,3px);} }
  @keyframes drift4 { 0%,100%{transform:translate(0,0);} 50%{transform:translate(-2px,-2px);} }
  @keyframes pulse { 0%,100%{transform:scale(1);} 50%{transform:scale(1.01);} }

  .electron{ animation-timing-function:ease-in-out; animation-iteration-count:infinite; transform-box: fill-box; transform-origin: center; }
  .electron.off{ animation-play-state:paused; }
  .sphere.pulse-anim{ animation:pulse 3s ease-in-out infinite; transform-box: fill-box; transform-origin:center; }
  .sphere.off{ animation-play-state:paused; }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="wrap">
  <h1>Thomson's plum pudding model</h1>
  <p class="sub">An animated look at the atomic model proposed after the discovery of the electron</p>

  <div class="card">
    <svg width="100%" viewBox="0 0 680 460" role="img" aria-label="Diagram of the plum pudding model showing negative electrons scattered inside a sphere of positive charge">
      <defs>
        <marker id="arrow" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="8" refY="5" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" orient="auto-start-reverse">
          <path d="M2 1L8 5L2 9" fill="none" stroke="#1a56b0" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
        </marker>
      </defs>

      <circle class="sphere pulse-anim" cx="340" cy="210" r="150" fill="#ffffff" stroke="#111111" stroke-width="2"/>

      <g class="t" font-size="20" fill="#111">
        <text x="270" y="100">+</text>
        <text x="380" y="95">+</text>
        <text x="230" y="150">+</text>
        <text x="420" y="140">+</text>
        <text x="300" y="170">+</text>
        <text x="250" y="220">+</text>
        <text x="410" y="215">+</text>
        <text x="340" y="250">+</text>
        <text x="280" y="290">+</text>
        <text x="390" y="285">+</text>
        <text x="240" y="270">+</text>
        <text x="430" y="260">+</text>
        <text x="320" y="120">+</text>
        <text x="360" y="310">+</text>
      </g>

      <g>
        <g class="electron" style="animation:drift1 2.6s infinite;"><circle cx="290" cy="110" r="10" fill="#2e7d32" stroke="#111" stroke-width="1"/><line x1="284" y1="110" x2="296" y2="110" stroke="#fff" stroke-width="2"/></g>
        <g class="electron" style="animation:drift2 3.1s infinite;"><circle cx="400" cy="120" r="10" fill="#2e7d32" stroke="#111" stroke-width="1"/><line x1="394" y1="120" x2="406" y2="120" stroke="#fff" stroke-width="2"/></g>
        <g class="electron" style="animation:drift3 2.9s infinite;"><circle cx="260" cy="180" r="10" fill="#2e7d32" stroke="#111" stroke-width="1"/><line x1="254" y1="180" x2="266" y2="180" stroke="#fff" stroke-width="2"/></g>
        <g class="electron" style="animation:drift4 3.4s infinite;"><circle cx="340" cy="170" r="10" fill="#2e7d32" stroke="#111" stroke-width="1"/><line x1="334" y1="170" x2="346" y2="170" stroke="#fff" stroke-width="2"/></g>
        <g class="electron" style="animation:drift1 3.3s infinite;"><circle cx="430" cy="185" r="10" fill="#2e7d32" stroke="#111" stroke-width="1"/><line x1="424" y1="185" x2="436" y2="185" stroke="#fff" stroke-width="2"/></g>
        <g class="electron" style="animation:drift2 2.7s infinite;"><circle cx="220" cy="230" r="10" fill="#2e7d32" stroke="#111" stroke-width="1"/><line x1="214" y1="230" x2="226" y2="230" stroke="#fff" stroke-width="2"/></g>
        <g class="electron" style="animation:drift3 3.0s infinite;"><circle cx="300" cy="230" r="10" fill="#2e7d32" stroke="#111" stroke-width="1"/><line x1="294" y1="230" x2="306" y2="230" stroke="#fff" stroke-width="2"/></g>
        <g class="electron" style="animation:drift4 2.8s infinite;"><circle cx="390" cy="235" r="10" fill="#2e7d32" stroke="#111" stroke-width="1"/><line x1="384" y1="235" x2="396" y2="235" stroke="#fff" stroke-width="2"/></g>
        <g class="electron" style="animation:drift1 3.2s infinite;"><circle cx="250" cy="290" r="10" fill="#2e7d32" stroke="#111" stroke-width="1"/><line x1="244" y1="290" x2="256" y2="290" stroke="#fff" stroke-width="2"/></g>
        <g class="electron" style="animation:drift2 3.5s infinite;"><circle cx="345" cy="300" r="10" fill="#2e7d32" stroke="#111" stroke-width="1"/><line x1="339" y1="300" x2="351" y2="300" stroke="#fff" stroke-width="2"/></g>
        <g class="electron" style="animation:drift3 2.6s infinite;"><circle cx="420" cy="280" r="10" fill="#2e7d32" stroke="#111" stroke-width="1"/><line x1="414" y1="280" x2="426" y2="280" stroke="#fff" stroke-width="2"/></g>
        <g class="electron" style="animation:drift4 3.1s infinite;"><circle cx="310" cy="330" r="10" fill="#2e7d32" stroke="#111" stroke-width="1"/><line x1="304" y1="330" x2="316" y2="330" stroke="#fff" stroke-width="2"/></g>
        <g class="electron" style="animation:drift1 2.9s infinite;"><circle cx="390" cy="335" r="10" fill="#2e7d32" stroke="#111" stroke-width="1"/><line x1="384" y1="335" x2="396" y2="335" stroke="#fff" stroke-width="2"/></g>
        <g class="electron" id="labelElectron" style="animation:drift2 3.0s infinite;"><circle cx="460" cy="160" r="10" fill="#2e7d32" stroke="#111" stroke-width="1"/><line x1="454" y1="160" x2="466" y2="160" stroke="#fff" stroke-width="2"/></g>
      </g>

      <line x1="520" y1="70" x2="465" y2="150" stroke="#1a56b0" stroke-width="1.5" marker-end="url(#arrow)"/>
      <text class="t" x="500" y="56" fill="#1a56b0">electron</text>

      <text class="ts" x="340" y="392" text-anchor="middle">sphere of positive charge</text>

      <rect x="558" y="436" width="112" height="20" fill="#111111"/>
      <text class="watermark" x="664" y="450" text-anchor="end" fill="#ffffff" style="opacity:1;">www.sumitkonar.com</text>
    </svg>

    <div class="controls">
      <button id="toggleBtn" onclick="toggleAnim()">Pause animation</button>
      <span class="hint">Electrons drift within the positively charged sphere</span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="card">
    <h2>What the plum pudding model says</h2>
    <p>
      After Thomson discovered the electron in 1897, he needed a new way to picture the atom.
      Since electrons are negatively charged and atoms overall are neutral, there had to be
      positive charge somewhere too, balancing things out.
    </p>
    <p>
      Thomson proposed that an atom was a sphere of positive charge, with tiny negative
      electrons scattered through it &mdash; a bit like plums sitting inside a pudding, which is
      where the model gets its name. There was no dense nucleus in this picture. The positive
      charge was thought to be spread evenly throughout the whole atom, with electrons free to
      sit anywhere inside it.
    </p>
    <p>
      This model didn't last long. Just over a decade later, Ernest Rutherford's gold foil
      experiment showed that positive charge is actually concentrated in a tiny, dense nucleus
      at the centre of the atom, not spread out evenly. That discovery replaced the plum pudding
      model with the nuclear model of the atom still used today.
    </p>
  </div>
</div>

<script>
let running = true;
function toggleAnim(){
  running = !running;
  document.querySelectorAll('.electron').forEach(el => el.classList.toggle('off', !running));
  document.querySelector('.sphere').classList.toggle('off', !running);
  document.getElementById('toggleBtn').textContent = running ? 'Pause animation' : 'Start animation';
}
</script>
</body>
</html>
